cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Numerical dosimetric analysis of low-energy positrons in living
  biological samples — supporting code
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated journal article
  using the metadata under "preferred-citation".
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of a numerical framework that couples low-energy
  positron transport to a time-resolved radiobiological model, in order to
  quantify the absorbed dose and the cellular surviving fraction during
  depth-resolved Positron Annihilation Spectroscopy (PAS) of living
  biological samples. Mass collision stopping powers for a liver
  sinusoidal endothelial monolayer are computed with the Berger-Seltzer
  formulation over 5-100 keV, and dose is propagated through a
  Linear-Quadratic survival model extended with the Lea-Catcheside
  protraction factor and a phenomenological FLASH sparing factor, for
  continuous, pulsed and trap-based bunched beam regimes.
keywords:
  - positron annihilation spectroscopy
  - dosimetry
  - biomedicine
  - linear-quadratic model
  - Lea-Catcheside protraction factor
  - FLASH effect
  - slow positron beam
